the toy companies designers prepare a  sketch of the figurine showing not just  the physical characteristics such as  size colors and textures but also the  body pose and facial expression once the  sketch is finalized modelers use  specialized software to transform it  into a drawing for a three-dimensional  model then a 3d printer produces a model  in plastic the company also employs  modelers who work the traditional way  with Wax  the modeler makes the wax or plastic  model accordingly this Dino is divided  into four parts head body jaw and tongue  for each one workers now make a silicon  mold to cast several copies in hard  plastic that unlike the model material  can withstand repeated handling workers  fill a metal box they assemble around  the part with silicone about 12 hours  later when the silicone has cured they  cut it open and extract the model then  they use the vacated cavity to cast  several hard plastic copies of the part  one copy however goes to the companies  tool makers who use it to fabricate the  production mold they bury the copy and  putty but just up to the mid point next  they set the half-buried copy in a metal  form and fill to the top with plaster  once the plaster hardens they cure it in  an oven for about an hour then they  extract the putty to copy what's left in  the plaster is a cavity in the shape of  half the copy they now fill that cavity  with molten zinc alloy dwith copper  aluminum and magnesium once the metal  cools and solidifies they break the  plaster and voila one half of the  two-part metal production mold they  repeat the entire process to make the  other half  workers mount the two-part mold in an  injection molding machine the machine  shoots hot molten plastic into the mold  cavity immediately cools the plastic  enough to solidify it then ejects the  figurine or figurine part the plastic is  solid but still soft so they harden it  further in cold water the figurines then  go to the art department where artists  can paint them using both traditional  and air brushes once the paint dries  it's assembly time a worker glues the  Dinos tongue into the hinged jaw snaps  the jaw into the head then glues the  head to the body this ferocious beast is  ready to hit the playground
 

